{
  "_id": "tg-walk",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "heard the voice of the Lord God walking in the garden, Gen. 3:8 (Moses 4:14). shew them the way wherein they must walk, Ex. 18:20 (1 Kgs. 8:36; 2 Chr. 6:27). Israel walked forty years in the wilderness, Josh. 5:6. Satan … going to and fro in the earth, and from walking up and down in it, Job 1:7 (2:2). he walketh upon a snare, Job 18:8. he walketh in the circuit of heaven, Job 22:14. though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, Ps. 23:4. I will walk in mine integrity, Ps. 26:11. We … walked unto the house of God, Ps. 55:14. Oh that … Israel had walked in my ways, Ps. 81:13. feet have they, but they walk not, Ps. 115:7. I will walk at liberty, Ps. 119:45. Though I walk in the midst of trouble, Ps. 138:7. That thou mayest walk in the way of good men, Prov. 2:20. I have seen … princes walking as servants, Eccl. 10:7. I should not walk in the way of this people, Isa. 8:11. redeemed shall walk there, Isa. 35:9. they shall walk, and not faint, Isa. 40:31 (D&C 89:20). when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned, Isa. 43:2. is not in man that walketh to direct his steps, Jer. 10:23. four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, Dan. 3:25. those that walk in pride he is able to abase, Dan. 4:37. Can two walk together, except they be agreed, Amos 3:3. Thou didst walk through the sea, Hab. 3:15. sent to walk to and fro through the earth, Zech. 1:10. they shall walk up and down in his name, Zech. 10:12.",
