    {
      "text": "Arise, and walk, Matt. 9:5 (Mark 2:9; Luke 5:23). lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, Matt. 11:5 (Luke 7:22). unclean spirit … walketh through dry places, Matt. 12:43 (Luke 11:24). disciples saw him walking on the sea, Matt. 14:26 (Mark 6:49; John 6:19). multitude wondered, when they saw … lame to walk, Matt. 15:31. Why walk not thy disciples according to the tradition, Mark 7:5. I see men as trees, walking, Mark 8:24. I must walk to day … for it cannot be that a prophet perish out of Jerusalem, Luke 13:33. take up thy bed, and walk, John 5:8. Jesus walked in Galilee, John 7:1. any man walk in the day, he stumbleth not, John 11:9. Walk while ye have the light, John 12:35. thou girdedst thyself, and walkedst whither thou wouldest, John 21:18. some, which think of us as if we walked according to the flesh, 2 Cor. 10:2. God hath before ordained that we should walk in them, Eph. 2:10. walk not as other Gentiles, Eph. 4:17. walk as children of light, Eph. 5:8. See then that ye walk circumspectly, Eph. 5:15. mark them which walk so as ye have us for an ensample, Philip. 3:17. walk honestly toward them that are without, 1 Thes. 4:12. withdraw yourselves from every brother that walketh disorderly, 2 Thes. 3:6. devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, 1 Pet. 5:8.",
